-- Computes CRC32C for corruption detection; it is not a cryptographic digest.
public define state as opaque.
public use "checksum" function compute(value sequence of constant byte) giving unsigned 32.
public use "checksum" function begin giving failable pointer to state.
public use "checksum" function update(state pointer to state, value sequence of constant byte) giving nothing.
public use "checksum" function result(state pointer to state) giving unsigned 32.
public use "checksum" function close(state pointer to state) giving nothing.
